	(descr "Vishay LTO 50 thick-film power resistor (TO-220 style, isolated ceramic back) laid FLAT, ceramic face down in a Wakefield 272-AB channel heat sink (separate footprint Library:Heatsink_Wakefield_272-AB = HS1; the LTO 50 hole sits on HS1 pad 1). Dimensioned for the LTO 50 only (hole to lead-end face 13.0 mm). Leads formed 90 deg toward the ceramic side like Vishay LTO 100 TB8: straight 4.2 mm from the body, inner radius 1.2 mm, outer lead face 6.0 +-0.5 mm from the body -> lead centre 5.7 mm from the body, pad row 18.7 mm from the hole. Plated slots 1.5 x 3.0 mm (JLCPCB: plated slot length >= 2x width; lead 0.8 x 0.6 mm) take +-1.08 mm along the lead axis (+-1.04 mm at the -0.08 mm slot tolerance) and +-0.35 mm across. Body, hole and leads on F.Fab only; courtyard = pads + formed-lead zone up to the HS1 courtyard (the body lies inside HS1). https://www.vishay.com/docs/50050/lto50.pdf")
	(tags "LTO50 LTO 50 TO-220-2 horizontal flat power resistor heatsink 272-AB")
